                <pb facs="0278" n="193" sameAs="frus:frus1919v02/pg193"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">422.11G93/1042: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Ecuador</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Hartman</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Acting Secretary of
                            State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Quito</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-07-17T09:00:00-05:14"><hi rendition="#italic">July 17, 1919,
                                9 a.m.</hi></date><lb/>[<hi rendition="#italic">Received July 18,
                            5.25 a.m.</hi>]</dateline></opener>
                <p>Railway manager informs me that Ecuadorean Government has remitted the 10,000
                    pounds mentioned in my July 14, 4 p.m., and that President of Ecuador informed
                    him yesterday that Ecuadorean Consul General in New York has been instructed to
                    remit 5,000 pounds additional.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hartman</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
